      "page": {
        "kind": "Text",
        "text": "Welcome to **Mathlore**, a structured mathematical library and encyclopedia\nconstructed from first principles using the **Mathlingua** language.\n\nThe goal of Mathlore is to provide an accessible, rigorous, and structurally-checked\nfoundation for mathematics—spanning symbolic logic, axiomatic set theory, relations,\nfunction theory, number systems, and abstract algebra."
      },
      "source": "Text: \"Welcome to **Mathlore**, a structured mathematical library and encyclopedia\nconstructed from first principles using the **Mathlingua** language.\n\nThe goal of Mathlore is to provide an accessible, rigorous, and structurally-checked\nfoundation for mathematics—spanning symbolic logic, axiomatic set theory, relations,\nfunction theory, number systems, and abstract algebra.\n\"\nId: \"7bbe5cda-edfe-4c9a-8894-a3573ca752ac\"",
      "sections": [
        {
          "label": "Text",
          "inline_argument": "\"Welcome to **Mathlore**, a structured mathematical library and encyclopedia\nconstructed from first principles using the **Mathlingua** language.\n\nThe goal of Mathlore is to provide an accessible, rigorous, and structurally-checked\nfoundation for mathematics—spanning symbolic logic, axiomatic set theory, relations,\nfunction theory, number systems, and abstract algebra.\n\"",
